Unreleased
==========

Symbolic trie
-------------

- Added an in-memory symbolic-trie index with configurable 2-, 4-, or 8-way
  fanout, leaf capacity, sampled root splitting, and entropy × variance-based
  splits.
- Stores MBRs and selects split dimensions across the full transform word
  (up to 128 dimensions, capped by the series length); split selection uses
  the leading 64 dimensions by default and can be overridden independently.
  Record lower bounds use the leading 16 dimensions.
- Supports SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words, including integer input files,
  optional z-normalization, and query-specific symbolic lower-bound tables.
- Uses node-MBR pruning plus best-first leaf scans, ordered by record lower
  bounds, with exact-distance early abandonment.  An optional disjoint
  leaf-MBR suffix contribution strengthens record bounds beyond the first
  16 dimensions (`--trie-record-mbr-suffix-bound`).
- Avoids a redundant full root-MBR scan for split tries by merging the MBRs
  already produced during root partitioning.
- Added an optional post-build, flat k-means directory inside large SFA, PISA,
  and SPARTAN trie leaves (`--trie-leaf-kmeans K`).  Cluster MBR bounds prune
  groups before their records are scanned, without changing the main trie;
  eligible leaves are clustered in parallel during construction.
- Optional `--trie-leaf-centroid-bound` adds a conservative raw-series
  centroid/radius triangle bound to those k-means groups. It is opt-in and
  reports its aggregate pruning contribution in the query summary.
- Provides batch and single-query parallel modes with configurable worker and
  queue counts, plus construction, coverage, and per-phase query timings.
- Reports split occupancy, non-empty-child, and largest-child diagnostics to
  make fanout experiments directly comparable.

SIMD and distance kernels
-------------------------

- Improved BSF-aware SIMD Euclidean-distance and symbolic lower-bound paths,
  including register-only horizontal reductions and alignment selection
  outside the vector loop where supported.
- Added scalar-reference coverage for exact distance and lower-bound SIMD
  kernels, plus a target-CPU exact-distance microbenchmark.
- Configuration output now identifies the SIMD instruction set in use (or
  states when no SIMD ISA was compiled in).

Sampling
--------

- Reworked SPARTAN uniform and random binning samples to read contiguous
  blocks instead of seeking separately for every sampled record.  This avoids
  the severe random-I/O slowdown on large datasets.
- Replaced SPARTAN, SFA, and PISA linear bin-boundary scans during
  symbolization with equivalent binary searches.

iSAX
----

- Added dynamic, variance-driven root-cardinality splitting for symbolic
  transforms and support for SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words.
- Added full-word node MBR pruning and transform-specific lower bounds,
  including SIMD-capable exact-distance paths where available.
- Improved parallel index construction and hybrid query scheduling, including
  configurable worker/queue counts and robust queue ownership.
- Unified iSAX and trie benchmark summaries, CSV logs, coverage reporting,
  construction timings, and optional per-phase query profiling.

Benchmark runners
-----------------

- `run_dataset.sh` now prints compact K/M/G configuration counts and an
  end-of-run table of query work, coverage, and wall time for all methods run.
- `run_suite.sh` accepts `--index-type isax|trie` to run a regular suite across
  all configured datasets with either layout.
- iSAX runner methods use variance-driven root cardinalities by default;
  trie MBR/split dimensions follow each dataset's coefficient setting and can
  be overridden with `--trie-mbr-dims` (16--128, capped by series length);
  split-choice width is independently configurable with `--trie-split-dims`
  and defaults to 32 dimensions in benchmark runners. Trie fanout is configurable with
  `--trie-fanout 2|4|8`.
- Trie suite and dataset runners forward the record-MBR suffix and leaf
  k-means options.  Runner and MESSI logs again default to
  `$HOME/MESSI_logs` (overridable with `MESSI_LOG_ROOT`).

Build integration
-----------------

- Kept generated Autotools configuration headers out of source control, so
  local configure/build output does not pollute commits.
